<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simele massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1933</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Simele massacre was the killing of Assyrian villagers by the Iraqi army in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> in August 1933, centred on the town of Simele near Dohuk. It followed armed clashes with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> seeking autonomy under their patriarch, and estimates of the dead range from several hundred to about 3,000. It was the first major crisis of independent Iraq and is a defining event in modern Assyrian memory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simele-massacre.jpg" alt="Simele massacre" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No. 30 (B) Squadron, Royal Air Force · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Batarshah_in_northern_Iraq,_an_Assyrian_village_destroyed_by_Arabs_and_Kurds_during_the_disturbances_of_August_1933.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
